diff --git a/ohos/README.md b/ohos/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..3a0dc580fd2554b9447596c8c61a954f3b9233f3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ohos/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,156 @@
+# HarmonyOS / in-process QEMU core (`VW_ENABLE_QEMU_OHOS`)
+
+This directory contains the HarmonyOS-independent, embeddable QEMU core work
+for VirtualWorld.  Everything here is **opt-in** and isolated behind the meson
+option `vw_enable_qemu_ohos` (default: **disabled**), so a normal build of this
+tree produces exactly the stock QEMU targets — including a working
+`qemu-system-aarch64` — with no extra in-process/OHOS target.
+
+## What is here
+
+| File | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `vw_embedded_stubs.c` | Non-spawning replacements for the symbols defined by the four non-core QEMU objects that own every host process-spawning call in the system-emulator link closure (`block/os-posix.c`, `migration/cpr-exec.c`, `net/tap.c`, `semihosting/syscalls.c`).  Operations that upstream performed by spawning a process fail cleanly with a structured `Error` (or a guest-visible `ENOSYS` for semihosting). |
+
+The in-process entry layer itself lives in `../qemu-inprocess/`
+(`qemu_inprocess.c` / `qemu_inprocess.h`); the acceptance harness is
+`../qemu-inprocess/lifecycle_harness.c`.
+
+## Build gate (meson option)
+
+`meson_options.txt`:
+
+```meson
+option('vw_enable_qemu_ohos', type: 'boolean', value: false,
+       description: 'build the VirtualWorld HarmonyOS/in-process QEMU core (default: disabled)')
+```
+
+The configure summary shows the gate:
+
+```
+VirtualWorld in-process (OHOS)
+  QEMU OHOS in-process build (vw_enable_qemu_ohos)  NO
+```
+
+`meson.build` builds the per-softmmu-target in-process archive and harness only
+when the option is enabled:
+
+```meson
+if target.endswith('-softmmu') and get_option('vw_enable_qemu_ohos')
+  # qemu-inprocess-<target>            static archive (qemu_inprocess.c + all target objects)
+  # qemu-inprocess-linkcheck-<target>  link-closure check executable
+  # qemu-inprocess-lifecycle-<target>  same-PID lifecycle acceptance harness
+endif
+```
+
+### Spawn-free at the meson level (option-enabled configuration)
+
+In the plain upstream source list, four non-core objects are pulled into *every*
+system-emulator link (including the meson `qemu-inprocess-lifecycle-<target>`)
+because the objects belong to the shared `system_ss` / `blockdev_ss` source sets:
+
+```
+libblockdev.a.p/os-posix.c.o            fork
+libsystem.a.p/migration_cpr-exec.c.o    execvp
+libsystem.a.p/net_tap.c.o               execv, fork
+libsystem.a.p/semihosting_syscalls.c.o  system
+```
+
+With `vw_enable_qemu_ohos=true` those four files are **not compiled at all**
+(`meson.build`, `migration/meson.build`, `net/meson.build`,
+`semihosting/meson.build` conditionally omit them) and `ohos/vw_embedded_stubs.c`
+is compiled into `libsystem.a` in their place.  The resulting configuration is
+the OHOS/embedded variant of the tree: every executable built from it (the
+stock emulator targets and the in-process lifecycle target alike) contains no
+`fork`/`exec*`/`posix_spawn`/`system`/`popen`, verified with `nm`/`objdump` in
+`build-qemu-inprocess/evidence/`.
+
+The option is POSIX-host only: with the option enabled on Windows/emscripten
+the build stops at configure time with an explicit error (those hosts do not
+have the POSIX host-process helpers this gate replaces).
+
+With the option **disabled** (the default, required for every normal QEMU
+host build) none of the above changes: the four stock sources are compiled
+exactly as upstream, `ohos/vw_embedded_stubs.c` is not compiled, and no
+`qemu-inprocess-*` target is created.
+
+### Default build (gate disabled — the regression that must stay green)
+
+```sh
+mkdir -p build-ohos-default && cd build-ohos-default
+../configure --target-list=aarch64-softmmu --disable-docs --disable-tools \
+    --disable-guest-agent --disable-bsd-user --disable-linux-user \
+    --disable-slirp --disable-capstone --disable-libssh --disable-gtk \
+    --disable-sdl --disable-cocoa --disable-spice --disable-vnc \
+    --disable-curses --disable-vte --disable-brlapi --disable-kvm \
+    -Dpvg=disabled
+ninja qemu-system-aarch64          # stock binary, no qemu-inprocess-* target
+```
+
+(`-Dpvg=disabled` is required on hosts whose macOS SDK marks
+`PGNewDeviceWithDescriptor` obsoleted-in-27.0; this is unrelated to the OHOS
+work and affects any from-scratch macOS build.)
+
+### Enabled build (spawn-free in-process lifecycle target)
+
+```sh
+mkdir -p build-ohos-enabled && cd build-ohos-enabled
+../configure --target-list=aarch64-softmmu -Dvw_enable_qemu_ohos=true \
+    [same --disable-* flags as above]
+ninja qemu-inprocess-lifecycle-aarch64
+# equivalent, after a normal configure:
+#   meson configure . -Dvw_enable_qemu_ohos=true
+# then verify the closure:
+nm -u -j qemu-inprocess-lifecycle-aarch64 | sed 's/^_//' \
+  | grep -xE 'fork|vfork|execv|execve|execvp|execvpe|execl|execle|execlp|posix_spawn|posix_spawnp|system|popen'   # no output
+./qemu-inprocess-lifecycle-aarch64   # malformed battery + 100 same-PID rounds
+```
+
+(`-Dmesonoptname=val` is QEMU configure's documented passthrough to meson; the
+option is not added to the generated `--enable-*` configure switches, so it is
+only reachable through the meson option itself.)
+
+## Shipped embedded harness (out-of-tree link, independent cross-check)
+
+`build-qemu-inprocess/build_ohos_target.py` + `link_ohos_embedded.py` build the
+archived embedded harness `qemu-core-embedded-ohos` from the proven gold ninja
+link command, independently of the meson wiring: they remove the same four
+non-core objects from the closure, compile the same `vw_embedded_stubs.c`, and
+fail the build if a dropped object is still present or a banned symbol appears
+in the final binary.
+
+```sh
+cd build-qemu-inprocess
+python3 build_ohos_target.py                 # compile stubs + link + verify
+#   -> qemu-core-embedded-ohos
+#   -> evidence/spawn-symbols-after-removal.txt   (nm/otool/objdump verdict)
+
+QEMU_INPROCESS_ROUNDS=20 QEMU_INPROCESS_SKIP_BATTERY=1 \
+    ./qemu-core-embedded-ohos                # lifecycle gate, same PID
+```
+
+## Behaviour of the stubs
+
+* `-daemonize`, `-runas`, `-run-with chroot=…`: structured error, no fork/
+  chroot/setuid; `-daemonize` is already rejected earlier by the in-process
+  `system/vl.c` entry point.
+* CPR exec migration (`cpr_exec_*`): structured `Error`; exec migration is not
+  available in an embedded process.
+* `tap` / `bridge` netdevs: structured `Error`; the tap/bridge helper would
+  have spawned a process.
+* Semihosting file/shell calls: guest-visible `ENOSYS`; `SYS_SYSTEM` never
+  reaches `system()`.
+* Pure-local hooks (`os_set_line_buffering`, `os_setup_post`, `os_mlock`, …):
+  documented no-ops safe for a library running inside a host application.
+
+## Lifecycle harness diagnostics (development only, inert by default)
+
+The acceptance path is unchanged by these knobs; they exist to make the rare
+teardown failure reproducible without a debugger.
+
+| env | effect |
+| --- | --- |
+| `VW_DUMP_STACKS=1` | on the 120 s watchdog timeout, every thread prints its own backtrace in-process (Mach `task_threads` + `thread_get_state` + `backtrace()`), then the harness aborts.  No child process is used. |
+| `VW_BT_ON_CRASH=1` | print a backtrace from the fatal-signal handler (SIGABRT/SIGBUS/SIGILL). |
+| `VW_BATTERY_ONLY=<idx>` | run only one malformed-battery entry (attribution only). |
+| `VW_BATTERY8_S=1` | append `-S` to warning-only battery entry 8 (attribution only). |
diff --git a/ohos/vw_embedded_stubs.c b/ohos/vw_embedded_stubs.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5cbd99d47737561dac213cd8ba39c42432525dc6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ohos/vw_embedded_stubs.c
@@ -0,0 +1,360 @@
+/*
+ * vw_embedded_stubs.c - non-spawning replacements for the four non-core QEMU
+ * objects that are removed from the embedded (VW_ENABLE_QEMU_OHOS) link
+ * closure.
+ *
+ * Background
+ * ==========
+ * Upstream QEMU puts four non-core objects in the system-emulator link
+ * closure.  Each of them is the *only* source of a host process-spawning API
+ * in the embedded harness binary:
+ *
+ *   libblockdev.a.p/os-posix.c.o           fork() (daemonize)
+ *   libsystem.a.p/migration_cpr-exec.c.o   execvp() (CPR exec migration)
+ *   libsystem.a.p/net_tap.c.o              execv()/fork() (tap helper, bridge)
+ *   libsystem.a.p/semihosting_syscalls.c.o system() (SYS_SYSTEM semihosting)
+ *
+ * The embedded/OHOS build removes those four objects from the link closure.
+ * This file provides the subset of their symbols that the *remaining* closure
+ * still references, so the link resolves without re-introducing the objects:
+ *
+ *   os-posix:    os_set_line_buffering, os_setup_early_signal_handling,
+ *                os_set_proc_name, os_setup_signal_handling,
+ *                os_set_daemonize, os_daemonize, os_set_runas, os_set_chroot,
+ *                os_setup_limits, os_setup_post, os_mlock
+ *   cpr-exec:    cpr_exec_init, cpr_exec_output, cpr_exec_input,
+ *                cpr_exec_persist_state, cpr_exec_has_state,
+ *                cpr_exec_unpersist_state, cpr_exec_unpreserve_fds
+ *   net_tap:     net_init_tap, net_init_bridge, tap_enable, tap_disable
+ *   semihosting: semihost_sys_{open,close,read,read_gf,write,write_gf,lseek,
+ *                isatty,flen,remove,rename,system} (guest-visible ENOSYS)
+ *
+ * Behaviour rules
+ * ===============
+ *   * nothing here may create a process, signal the host, chroot, setuid or
+ *     terminate the host (no fork, exec-family, system, popen/exit/abort);
+ *   * operations that upstream would have performed by spawning a process
+ *     fail cleanly with a structured Error (Error **errp) where the API has
+ *     one, with a guest-visible ENOSYS for the semihosting calls, and with a
+ *     structured error_report for the legacy void APIs;
+ *   * purely local operations that are safe in an embedded process (line
+ *     buffering, no-op signal setup, memory locking) are implemented as
+ *     documented no-ops or one-line local operations.
+ *
+ * This file is part of the HarmonyOS/in-process build gate
+ * (VW_ENABLE_QEMU_OHOS) and is only compiled when that gate is enabled.
+ * It is NOT a standalone QEMU source file: it must be compiled with the same
+ * flags/include map as system/vl.c (see build-qemu-inprocess/build_ohos_target.py).
+ *
+ * SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
+ */
+
+#include "qemu/osdep.h"
+#include "qemu/error-report.h"
+#include "qapi/error.h"
+#include "system/os-posix.h"
